<title>USA: Gaylord unit names Whittaker president.</title>
<headline>Gaylord unit names Whittaker president.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gaylord Entertainment Co said Monday that Bob Whittaker, vice president and general manager of its Grand Ole Opry Group, will replace Hal Durham, who is retiring as president of the group.</p>
<p>Whittaker replaces Durham as president on November 1, the company said.</p>
<p>In addition to producing the Grand Ole Opry, the Grand Ole Opry Group produces live shows at the Opryland theme park and produces more than 1,200 performances for a variety of shows.</p>
</text>
